WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.831
- I think this should be pretty easy.

00:00:01.831 --> 00:00:06.224
(playful music)

00:00:12.297 --> 00:00:17.297
(gentle music)

00:00:18.186 --> 00:00:19.488
This is harder than I thought.

00:00:19.488 --> 00:00:21.930
- I think my son was trying to trick me.

00:00:21.930 --> 00:00:24.896
- I don't know, this is tough.

00:00:24.896 --> 00:00:26.378
- This one is Zeke's.

00:00:26.378 --> 00:00:27.658
You can tell what it is,

00:00:27.658 --> 00:00:29.982
but it's also kind of sloppy.
(laughs)

00:00:29.982 --> 00:00:30.793
(buzzer)

00:00:30.793 --> 00:00:32.468
Oh, was it this one?

00:00:32.468 --> 00:00:33.118
- [Voiceover] Yeah.

00:00:33.118 --> 00:00:34.195
- Oh, that's so funny.

00:00:34.195 --> 00:00:36.584
- The clock that my son has in his bedroom

00:00:36.584 --> 00:00:39.069
is a digital clock, so I'm going to choose

00:00:39.069 --> 00:00:41.203
the only digital clock of the bunch.

00:00:41.203 --> 00:00:42.408
(bell rings)

00:00:42.408 --> 00:00:44.872
- The one with the most color on it.

00:00:44.872 --> 00:00:45.853
(bell rings)

00:00:45.853 --> 00:00:46.611
Yes!

00:00:46.611 --> 00:00:47.656
- This one.

00:00:47.656 --> 00:00:48.957
The reason why is because I know

00:00:48.957 --> 00:00:51.912
she knows what a clock
is, but I don't think

00:00:51.912 --> 00:00:53.907
she knows where the numbers go.

00:00:53.907 --> 00:00:54.952
(bell rings)

00:00:54.952 --> 00:00:56.247
She's my kid.

00:00:58.461 --> 00:01:01.107
- The one that looks most
like a type of creature

00:01:01.107 --> 00:01:03.613
he likes to make up is this one.

00:01:03.613 --> 00:01:04.819
(bell rings)

00:01:04.819 --> 00:01:05.991
- This one?

00:01:05.991 --> 00:01:06.823
(bell rings)

00:01:06.823 --> 00:01:07.729
(screams)

00:01:07.729 --> 00:01:08.977
- I feel like she would label it.

00:01:08.977 --> 00:01:09.724
Also, the mixed colors.

00:01:09.724 --> 00:01:10.755
(bell rings)

00:01:11.985 --> 00:01:13.519
- I'm gonna say this one.

00:01:13.519 --> 00:01:15.300
And I don't really have a reason.

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:16.142
I just think it is.

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:16.771
(buzzer)

00:01:16.771 --> 00:01:18.137
Is it this one?
(laughs)

00:01:18.137 --> 00:01:19.182
- [Voiceover] Yes, it is.

00:01:19.182 --> 00:01:21.529
- Oh, son, you're gonna kill me.

00:01:24.045 --> 00:01:25.485
- It's between these two.

00:01:25.485 --> 00:01:26.157
- This one?

00:01:26.157 --> 00:01:26.979
(buzzer)

00:01:26.979 --> 00:01:28.739
No!

00:01:28.739 --> 00:01:30.999
Oh my god, I can't believe I got it wrong.

00:01:30.999 --> 00:01:32.919
- I know that he can
draw better than this.

00:01:32.919 --> 00:01:35.085
So I think he was trying to trick me.

00:01:35.085 --> 00:01:35.959
I will guess this one.

00:01:35.959 --> 00:01:36.845
(bell rings)

00:01:37.895 --> 00:01:41.559
- I'm gonna say the
green one because I think

00:01:41.559 --> 00:01:43.372
she likes green apples more than red ones.

00:01:43.372 --> 00:01:44.791
(bell rings)

00:01:45.749 --> 00:01:46.816
- This is really hard.

00:01:46.816 --> 00:01:47.936
I think maybe this one?

00:01:47.936 --> 00:01:48.789
(bell rings)

00:01:48.789 --> 00:01:50.835
Thank you.
(chuckles)

00:01:50.835 --> 00:01:52.687
I love you, Zeke.

00:01:52.687 --> 00:01:54.319
Good worm in apple.

00:01:56.544 --> 00:01:59.285
- I am very surprised that
I got one of these wrong.

00:01:59.285 --> 00:02:02.122
- The surprise is that he
didn't try to trick me.

00:02:02.122 --> 00:02:04.746
I think he tried to use
some reverse psychology.

00:02:04.746 --> 00:02:06.581
- I felt like I was gonna know.

00:02:06.581 --> 00:02:10.645
It threw me off having two
kids at similar levels.

00:02:10.645 --> 00:02:12.896
- Zeke did throw me off a
little bit on his pictures.

00:02:12.896 --> 00:02:15.226
I don't know if he did it on purpose

00:02:15.226 --> 00:02:17.685
to try to trick me so
later on he could be like,

00:02:17.685 --> 00:02:18.752
"You know, you really hurt my feelings,

00:02:18.752 --> 00:02:21.536
"but some new Pokemon cards
would really make up for it."

00:02:21.536 --> 00:02:23.808
So I'm a little disappointed in myself.

00:02:23.808 --> 00:02:26.485
I might buy you some guilt
Pokemon cards after all.

00:02:26.485 --> 00:02:28.106
(laughs)

00:02:28.106 --> 00:02:29.291
Oh, man.

